# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Why this is not the usual Windows setup: the seven code generators under
# NewVersion/scripts/ write LF, and `npm run data:check` compares their output
# byte-for-byte against the committed files. With Git's default
# `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows, checkout rewrites those files to CRLF, every
# generated file then differs from what its generator produces, and the check
# fails on a clean tree — as it did the moment this repo was initialised.
#
# Forcing LF everywhere keeps generated and committed bytes identical on every
# platform. Editors on Windows handle LF fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Extracted SWF assets are binary; never touch them.
*.mp3 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ttf binary
*.swf binary

# JPEXS writes these; keep them exactly as extracted so the extraction stays
# byte-comparable against a fresh export.
SWFimported/** -text
